{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.632 acc, slightly below the RNA-only best (0.650/0.653), suggesting concat fusion of weak image features introduces noise. However, it remains unclear whether the image modality is fundamentally uninformative or whether the simple concat fusion is the bottleneck. Question: config_031 changes only the fusion strategy from concat to weighted, holding all other variables constant (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50). This isolates the fusion axis. If weighted fusion recovers performance toward or above 0.650, it indicates the image carries complementary signal that needs proper weighting, justifying further investment in image encoders (e.g., ViT-L). If it does not help, it strongly suggests ResNet50 image features are uninformative for this task, allowing us to deprioritize the image modality and focus budget on other axes. This is the most informative single-variable experiment because it directly resolves the key uncertainty about whether the image modality is worth pursuing, and the result will guide all subsequent multimodal decisions."
}

